{"full":"hf:kulibinai/cadena-stepwise-cad","spaceId":"kulibinai/cadena-stepwise-cad","name":"CADENA Stepwise CAD","source":"huggingface","description":"Turn a 3D mesh into a parametric CadQuery program","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"Python","topics":["gradio","region:us"],"technologies":["Python"],"likes":47,"created":"2026-08-04T07:19:04.000Z","updated":"2026-08-05T13:21:23.000Z","license":"mit","runtime":"RUNNING","appUrl":"https://kulibinai-cadena-stepwise-cad.hf.space/","demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/kulibinai/cadena-stepwise-cad","availability":"available","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T05:12:48.890Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-17T05:12:48.890Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-17T05:12:48.890Z","color":"#3c3250","ink":"#e4d4ff","symbol":"📐","overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Gradio demo for CADENA — a Qwen2-VL-2B policy that reverse-engineers a 3D mesh into a parametric CadQuery program, one operation at a time.","At each step the target mesh and the solid built so far are rendered into an eight-view collage (six axis-aligned orthographic views whose brightness encodes depth, plus two isometric views). The target occupies the green channel and the geometry built so far the red one, so what the policy reads is the residual. It emits the next CAD operation, the partial program is executed with OpenCASCADE, volumetric IoU against the target is measured, and the step is kept only if IoU improved.","The rollout mirrors inference/cadworker.py from zhemdi/cadena, with vLLM serving replaced by a local transformers generate call so it fits a single ZeroGPU slot."],"features":["Weights: kulibinai/cadena (CADENA-RL checkpoint)","Code: github.com/zhemdi/cadena (MIT) — cadgen/, utils/, rl/, visualization.py are vendored here unmodified","Benchmark: kulibinai/cadena-bench"],"sourceUrl":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/kulibinai/cadena-stepwise-cad/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"b33dac060bef9f88cb594a34276f5ad77eb3032b9e45f564ca40419b38465